WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.035 line:0%
MOUDI: I came here to the
United States a month ago,

00:00:03.135 --> 00:00:09.008 line:0%
after I escaped my country,
and I think it's time to expose

00:00:09.108 --> 00:00:10.643 line:7%
what's going on there.

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:14.047
[music playing]

00:00:25.758 --> 00:00:28.227 line:0%
The penalty in Saudi Arabia
for somebody like me,

00:00:28.327 --> 00:00:33.899 line:0%
who opposed the
government, is beheaded.

00:00:33.999 --> 00:00:36.469 line:0%
ARWA: There are so many things
that women can't do in Saudi,

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:37.804 line:7%
because it's law.

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:40.707 line:0%
They can't do anything without
a male guardian's consent.

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:42.308 line:0%
MOUDI: When I was in
Saudi Arabia, if I wanted

00:00:42.408 --> 00:00:44.777 line:0%
to even go to the
supermarket, I have to inform

00:00:44.877 --> 00:00:45.678 line:7%
everyone in the house.

00:00:45.778 --> 00:00:47.546 line:7%
DANAH: I couldn't drive.

00:00:47.646 --> 00:00:50.583 line:0%
My father wasn't even thinking
about teaching me how to drive,

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:52.017 line:7%
because it's against the law.

00:00:52.117 --> 00:00:55.087 line:0%
ARWA: The laws in Saudi are
doing that systematically

00:00:55.187 --> 00:00:56.589 line:7%
to discriminate against women.

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:57.757 line:7%
Nobody talks about it.

00:00:57.857 --> 00:01:01.093 line:0%
MOUDI: Guardianship
system-- it's a slavery.

00:01:01.193 --> 00:01:03.362 line:0%
It's the worst human
rights violation.

00:01:03.462 --> 00:01:07.299 line:0%
DANAH: Sometimes, you feel
like your life is worthless.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:11.237 line:0%
ARWA: I felt like I was
nothing but a commodity.

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:14.707 line:0%
What really scares me is that
I wouldn't get this asylum

00:01:14.807 --> 00:01:18.211 line:0%
and I would be returned,
and then I would die young,

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:21.548 line:0%
and that I would lose
everything I tried to build--

00:01:21.648 --> 00:01:23.516 line:7%
that I would just fail.

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:26.786
[music playing]

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:31.124 line:7%
MOUDI: I escaped in the night.

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:33.893 line:0%
ARWA: My father was still
awake, and he was watching TV.

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:35.728 line:0%
I was really scared
if he would notice

00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:37.930 line:7%
that I'm going out of my room.

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:40.400 line:0%
MOUDI: I was prepared
that, in any second,

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.102 line:7%
I'm going to be dead.

00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:45.371 line:0%
ARWA: I haven't heard my
parents' voice since I left

00:01:45.471 --> 00:01:47.707 line:7%
Saudi, and I wish I never do.

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:52.278 line:0%
DANAH: Girls back home,
they're suffering.

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:54.747 line:0%
And some of them,
they can't speak.

00:01:54.847 --> 00:01:59.452 line:0%
So since I'm here and I'm in
a free country, I can talk.

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:00.686 line:7%
I can help them.

00:02:00.786 --> 00:02:03.289 line:0%
ARWA: I felt extremely
scared when I first got here,

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:06.225 line:7%
and I still feel that same fear.

00:02:06.325 --> 00:02:08.795 line:7%
Will I be able to make it?

00:02:08.895 --> 00:02:11.997 line:7%
Or am I just going to fail?

00:02:12.097 --> 00:02:15.301
[music playing]

00:02:18.237 --> 00:02:23.209 line:0%
All I really want is just to
live normally without fear

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:25.778 line:0%
and not have to pretend
to be somebody else.

00:02:25.878 --> 00:02:27.080 line:7%
That's all I ever want.

00:02:32.117 --> 00:02:34.153
-Do you have your
work authorization?

00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:34.954
ARWA: Yes.

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:38.424 line:7%
-OK, thank you.

00:02:38.524 --> 00:02:40.860
[sniffling]

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:52.572 line:0%
ARWA: I feel like this is
what I've always wanted,

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:54.707 line:0%
ever since I've
decided that I don't

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:56.509 line:7%
want to live in Saudi anymore.

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:59.345 line:0%
But this is-- this is what
I've been working towards.

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:02.782 line:0%
I want to go back to a
17-year-old me and tell her,

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:06.218 line:7%
"You're going to do it."

00:03:06.318 --> 00:03:10.790 line:0%
I feel like I want to go and
just talk to other Saudi girls

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:14.193 line:0%
that go through this,
leaving their homes

00:03:14.293 --> 00:03:19.198 line:0%
and being ostracized by their
families, having no one.

00:03:19.298 --> 00:03:21.166 line:7%
You know, you can do it too.

00:03:21.266 --> 00:03:24.537
[music playing]

